    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27336" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lychnus</span></b>  (old Latinized form lucinus, Enn.; cf.
		Ritschl in Rhein. Mus. 10, p. 448 sq.), i, m.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λύχνος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a light, a lamp</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pendentes lychni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					5, 295</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lux alia est solis et lychnorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Cael. 28, 67</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 1, 726</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 1,
				520</span></i>.</div>
